// P03.22 review (R18): the plain code and the generic code decide every
// partial place by the same rule. Inputs/gen-generic-plain-table.py writes,
// for each pair (use kind x type argument kind: a value child with an
// inherited method, one with its own method, a tagged value, pointers to a
// tagged type and to a child, an untagged child and root, Unique / Shared /
// View of a tagged type, a plain struct, int, an abstract type, func types
// returning a tagged and an abstract type), the plain form and the generic
// form, checks both (with one body thread and with eight) and compares them
// pair by pair (the legend is in the script). The whole table is pinned
// here; the compiler before R18 fails it (14 pairs). P03.26 added the View
// rows (a View[T] in a signature, a result, a body, a closure, an alias and a
// @View generic struct): an instance whose T is a pointer kind or a view is
// refused as the written View is, with E0371 on both sides; the swap through
// *View[X] is a re-point on both sides (OWN-V1), so the table has no KNOWN
// rows left. The rows view-instance and ptr-instance (`View[Box[T]]`,
// `*Box[T]` in a signature) are refused for an abstract T as the plain
// `Box[Shape]` is (the compiler before P03.26 fails them, 2 pairs). The
// method rows write the signature of a method of a generic type (`func (r
// G[T]) m(x []T)`, also behind a pointer receiver and through a generic
// function that holds G[U]): G[Shape] is refused as the plain method
// signature is (the compiler before P03.26 accepts them and fails the table).
// The arg-, field-, fieldrec-, method-arg- and alias-arg- rows (R12) write a
// value of T only inside a type argument that the generic holds behind a
// pointer (`PBox[[]T]`, `PBox[Box[T]]`, `PBox[func(T)]`), in a signature, a
// field, a recursive type, a method signature and an alias: refused for an
// abstract T as the plain `PBox[[]Shape]` is (the compiler before R12 accepts
// them, 16 pairs); arg-held, arg-pointer, arg-bare and field-arg-pointer are
// the controls.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-generic-plain-table.py --gopp %gopp --out %t | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: args: 0=child-inherited 1=child-own 2=tagged 3=ptr-tagged 4=ptr-child 5=untagged-child 6=untagged-root 7=unique 8=shared 9=view 10=plain 11=int 12=abstract 13=func-tagged 14=func-abstract
